/**
 * Day 99 — Phase 5 item 7: globe refinement of the existing countries — South Korea (the Korean
 * peninsula, with Manchuria for Goguryeo and Balhae).
 *
 * Before this, Korea before 1815 was drawn only by three schematic rings — Silla (600–900), Goryeo
 * (940–1300) and Joseon (1420–1850) — so the peninsula was empty before 580, between 1310 and 1400,
 * and Goguryeo, Baekje, Gaya, Gojoseon, the Han commanderies, Balhae and the Later Three Kingdoms were
 * not drawn at all. This pack adds them and redraws Silla, Goryeo and Joseon from the same pieces
 * (same ids, so their timeline links stay). The nations layer draws Korea from 1815 (Joseon) and the two
 * Koreas from 1948; this pack has no keyframe after 1813.
 *
 * How it is built (docs/DATA.md, "Country-pack globe backfill"):
 *  - 25 pieces: Natural Earth 1:10m admin-1 provinces of North and South Korea (North and South
 *    Gyeongsang cut along 128.45°E/36.6°N and 128.5°E), southern Primorsky Krai (to 46.3°N), and
 *    copies of the China pack's Liaodong, Jilin (cut at 42.3°N) and Heilongjiang pieces, polygonized
 *    together so shared edges match. Generator: et-tools day99-pieces.py.
 *  - A polity is a dated list of pieces; every change is a one-year step.
 *  - Every polity has a certainty level and sources, and links the South Korea timeline items.
 * Not drawn (timeline items and pins only): Dangun's Gojoseon before the 4th century BCE; Buyeo, Okjeo,
 * Dongye and the Samhan (Mahan, Jinhan, Byeonhan) as states; Usan and Tamna (Jeju is not on the
 * globe's land); the Tang protectorates of Ungjin (660–671) and Andong (668–676); the Jurchens of the
 * north-east before Joseon; the Yuan's Ssangseong (1258–1356) and the Japanese occupation in the Imjin
 * War (1592–1598).
 */
